==Trivia==
* Fiend is a "corrupted" form of Yeti, allegedly caused by [[Mygame43 (Player)|mygame43]]. 
* The mutation takes heavy inspiration from the famous Street fighter, Akuma.
* It originally was going to have an event transformed boss, similar to [[Unbound Werewolf]] and [[Hellfire Gas (Raid Boss)|Hellfire Gas]], but it was strangely never added.
* "Fiend" means an evil spirit or demon in religion or mythology.
* Fiend's obtainment is the exact same as [[Werewolf]], both being in a gacha, with their bundles costing {{Robux|3,999}} and both costing {{Robux|1,500}} individually, the only difference being the event in which they are obtainable.
* Unlike [[Yeti]], [[Draco]]'s V2 [[Flash Step]] works while transformed.
* The sound effect when walking on [[water]] (Fiend’s Cursed Strider passive) uses the exact same sound effect as [[Yeti]]'s similar ability even though it creates whirls and not ice.
* This is the third fruit [[mutation]] to be released, the first being [[Werewolf]] while the second being [[Empyrean]].
* This is the second fruit [[mutation]] to have a skin, the first one being [[Empyrean]].
* Despite not being entirely related, the Fiend seems to be more similar to [[Tiger]], both being powerful fighters with flame-based attacks.
* Fiend's {{Skin|Runic}} [[skin]] is one of the first skins to fully change the transformation model, with the other one being [[Magnet|Arcsteel Magnet]].
* Fiend's {{Skin|Runic}} skin was originally named 'Sealed Fiend'

